<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rajah of Sarawak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1841–1946</span> · Also known as White Rajah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rajah of Sarawak was the title of the Brooke family, the 'White Rajahs', who ruled Sarawak in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a> from 1841 to 1946. The sultan of Brunei granted it to the English adventurer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-brooke">James Brooke</a> for helping put down a revolt, and it passed to his nephew Charles and then to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-vyner-brooke">Charles Vyner Brooke</a>, who ceded Sarawak to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rajah-of-sarawak.jpg" alt="Rajah of Sarawak" width="320" height="379" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_Raj_of_Sarawak.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
